§ `Division 6: standard choice forms`

-- A form due before 29 July 2005 for an employee employed on 1 July 2005.
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee was employed by the employer on 1 July 2005` (Date 1 7 2005) (Date 28 7 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee was employed by the employer on 1 July 2005` (Date 1 7 2005) (Date 29 7 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Within 28 days of the employee first commencing on 1 July 2026: 28 July or 29 July is the last day, depending on whether the first day counts.
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 28 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee gave the employer a written request` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 28 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employer became aware that there ceased to be any chosen fund because of subsection 32H(3) or (4)` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employer changed the fund it contributes to under subsection 32C(2)` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 28 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employer first became aware that it cannot contribute to the employer fund` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 28 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A form given before the trigger: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `a standard choice form is given in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a written request for a standard choice form is taken never to have been made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a written request for a standard choice form is taken never to have been made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
